Task 1 — controlled CPython authority for SearXNG

Why:
- releases and local preparation previously accepted loosely matched Python runtimes;
- the runtime/build ABI must share one controlled CPython minor;
- Node.js and CPython remain external host prerequisites.

Implementation:
- scripts/build/searxng-python-version.txt is the single operational build-version authority (3.14, LF enforced);
- exact CPython probe and bounded/symlink-safe authority reader;
- setup-python pinned by commit SHA in the matrix build job, after checkout and before Tauri;
- official macOS/Linux/Windows prerequisite commands;
- Linux installation is fail-closed around existing executables and explicitly pins UV_INSTALL_DIR and UV_PYTHON_BIN_DIR.

Review history:
- initial review found CRLF, invalid macOS package URL, PATH ordering, workflow-order and symlink-test gaps;
- re-review found Linux non-login shell visibility;
- final review found destructive ln -sfn and XDG directory divergence;
- all findings were corrected and mutation-tested;
- closure review: SPEC PASS / QUALITY PASS, 0 Critical, 0 Important, 0 Minor.

Evidence:
- task tests 24/24;
- release workflow contracts 37/37;
- npm run lint and npx tsc --noEmit green;
- mutations red for missing eol=lf, setup before checkout, removed symlink guard, Darwin divergence, destructive/foreign Linux destinations, and XDG bin divergence;
- Node artifact URLs returned HTTP 200 on 2026-08-20.

Limits:
- native clean Linux/Windows installations were not executed in this task;
- Python remains external and is not bundled.
